# Neighbours (theme n7): noise, borrowing, fences, pups and gardens, thin walls, help in hard times. The opener
# remembers what it was about (pair.mem.nb), the neighbour answers as they are and remembers how they took it
# (pair.mem.na: sorry, rebuff, joke, dodge, give, none, thanks, proud, grief, chat, glare, plead, promise), and the
# opener has the last word (town.close, in town7.talk). Every answer is keyed to what it answers, since a chain's
# later beats always take their best tier.

## The opener (pair.neighbours=yes)

rule n7_nb_noise
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say Was that your lot banging about at midnight? | Somebody on our side was dragging furniture till all hours. Yours? | I heard a crash from yours last night. All well? | You were singing again. Through the wall. At length.
remember pair: nb=noise 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_noise_pups
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes other.parent=yes other.age<=45
cooldown 2d
say Your pups were up with the birds. So was I, as it happens. | Which of yours has learnt to howl? Because they're very proud of it. | There's a small wolf throwing pebbles at my shutter. I think it's one of yours.
remember pair: nb=pups 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_borrow_ladder
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.neighbours=yes pair.band!=strangers
cooldown 3d
say You've still got my ladder, you know. | Is my ladder still leaning on your wall? Only I've a gutter to see to. | I'll want my ladder back before the frost. No hurry. Some hurry.
remember pair: nb=borrow 3d
remember pair: lent=ladder 7d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_borrow_pot
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.neighbours=yes pair.band!=strangers
cooldown 3d
say Did my good pot ever come back from yours? | I went to make a stew last night and found I'd no pot. Then I remembered where it was. | That pot of mine. The big one. Still at yours?
remember pair: nb=borrow 3d
remember pair: lent=pot 7d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_borrow_saw
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.neighbours=yes pair.band!=strangers
cooldown 3d
say I'll want my saw back before the wood comes in. | My saw. You remember my saw? Sharp, wooden handle, mine? | Have you finished with the saw? Only I've a shelf that won't put itself up.
remember pair: nb=borrow 3d
remember pair: lent=saw 7d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_borrow_ask
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say Could I borrow a cup of salt? I'll pay it back Restday. | You've not a spare candle? Ours went out mid-supper. | Lend me your barrow an hour? I'll bring it back cleaner than it went. | Have you a needle I could borrow? Mine's gone into the floor somewhere.
remember pair: nb=ask 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_ask_poor
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say I hate to ask. Could you spare a little meal till Restday? | You've not a bit of kindling? We're down to the chair legs. | If you've any bread going stale, we'd not say no.
remember pair: nb=ask 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_fence
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes here.region!=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say That fence of ours is leaning. Your way or mine, I can't tell. | There's a gap in the fence a pup could walk through. One did, this morning. | We should go halves on new posts for the fence.
remember pair: nb=fence 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_stair
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say The stair's not been swept. I think it's your week. | Someone left a bucket on the landing and I found it with my foot. | Who's been leaving fish heads on the stair? The cats are holding a meeting.
remember pair: nb=stair 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_garden
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes here.season=spring|summer
cooldown 3d
say Your beans are coming up lovely. Better than mine, curse you. | Your roses are over my wall. I'm not complaining, they smell nice. | What do you put on your cabbages? Mine look like lace.
remember pair: nb=garden 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_garden_autumn
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes here.season=autumn
cooldown 3d
say Your apples keep falling on my side. I've been eating them, I'm afraid. | Your pear tree's leaning right over my yard. Not that I mind the pears. | Shall we swap? My onions for some of your pears.
remember pair: nb=harvest 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_snow
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.weather|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes here.weather=snow
cooldown 1d
say I've cleared your step with mine. Don't thank me. Clear both tomorrow. | Your step was a sheet of ice. I've put some ash down on it. | Snowed in, the pair of us. Knock on the wall if you need anything.
remember pair: nb=help 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_washing
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.weather pair.neighbours=yes here.weather=rain|storm
cooldown 1d
say Your washing was still out. I took it in for you; it's on my chair. | Rain came on. I've thrown your sheets over my line under the eaves. | I got your washing in before the worst of it. Mostly.
remember pair: nb=help 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_walls
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say These walls are thin as paper. I know what you had for supper. | I can hear your kettle. I can hear your kettle thinking about it. | Whoever builds these places ought to live in one. Next to you.
remember pair: nb=walls 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_smell
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 3d
say What were you cooking last night? The whole row was drooling. | Something smells wonderful from yours. Fish? | Whatever's in your pot tonight, I'll trade you for it.
remember pair: nb=cooking 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_smell_trade
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes other.job=fisher|smith|crafter|miner|herder
cooldown 3d
say Your work boots are on the step and the cats are worshipping them. | I always know when you're home. I mean that kindly. Mostly. | Could you not bring quite so much of your work home in your fur?
remember pair: nb=trade 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_critter
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 3d
say Is that your cat on my roof every night, yowling? | There's a hen in my yard. It looks like one of yours. | Something's been at my scraps. I'm not saying it was one of yours.
remember pair: nb=critter 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_away
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes self.travelling=yes
cooldown 2d
say I'm off on the road a few days. Keep an eye on my door? | Will you feed the hens while I'm gone? There's a penny in it. | If anyone comes asking, I'm away and I've nothing worth taking.
remember pair: nb=away 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_new
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.band=strangers
cooldown 1d
say You'll be the new folk next door. Welcome. | We've not met. I'm the door to your left. The one with the squeaky hinge. | I saw the cart. Settling in? If you need a hammer, knock.
remember pair: nb=new 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_late
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes here.time=night
cooldown 2d
say You're in late. Courting, or working? | I saw your light still on. Can't sleep either? | Not to pry, but who was that at your door?
remember pair: nb=late 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

## Help in hard times, from next door

rule n7_nb_help_hungry
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes other.hungry=yes self.wealth!=destitute self.hungry=no
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I made too much stew. Take some before it spoils. You'd be doing me a favour. | There's half a loaf going hard on my table. Take it, go on. | Come and eat with us tonight. No, I'll not hear no.
remember pair: nb=charity 3d
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_help_poor
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes self.wealth=rich|comfortable other.wealth=destitute self.warmth!=cold
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say I've a sack of meal I'll never get through. Help me with it? | If it's the rent, come and see me before you see the landlord. | We've a ham hanging that'll go off before we get to the end of it. I'll send half round.
remember pair: nb=charity 3d
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_help_mourning
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.neighbours=yes other.mourning=kin
cooldown 1d
priority 3
say I've left a pie on your step. Don't thank me. Just eat it. | We're only next door. Knock if you can't bear the quiet. | I'll see to your hens this week. You see to yourself.
remember pair: nb=grief 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_help_hurt
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes other.injured=bad self.injured!=bad
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say I'll fetch your water till you're mended. No arguing. | You're not to climb that ladder like that. Give me the job. | I'll send broth round. Leave the door on the latch.
remember pair: nb=help 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_help_old
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes other.stage=old self.stage=adult|adolescent
cooldown 2d
say Let me carry that for you. | Shall I bring your wood in? It's going to be a cold one. | Anything from the market? I'm going anyway.
remember pair: nb=help 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_help_robbed
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.crime pair.neighbours=yes other.robbed=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 2
say I heard about your trouble. I'll keep my ears open, both of them. | I've a spare bolt for your door. I'll fit it tonight. | If they come back, bang on the wall. I'll come with the poker.
remember pair: nb=help 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_rumour_thief
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.rumour=thief
cooldown 3d
priority 1
say I've started locking my door. Nothing personal. | My good knife's gone missing. I don't suppose you've seen it? | Funny. Since you moved in, things wander off.
remember pair: nb=suspect 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_rumour_violent
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.rumour=violent
cooldown 3d
priority 1
say I heard shouting from yours again. Everyone all right in there? | The pups are scared to walk past your door. I'd like to know why. | Folk say you've a heavy paw. I'd not like to find out.
remember pair: nb=suspect 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_rich_to_poor
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes self.wealth=rich other.wealth=poor|destitute self.warmth=cold
cooldown 3d
say Your cart is in front of my gate again. | Might you keep your pups off my steps? They were just whitened. | We've guests tonight. I'd be grateful for a little quiet from your side.
remember pair: nb=snub 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_poor_to_rich
when concept=talk.smalltalk pair.neighbours=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute other.wealth=rich
cooldown 3d
say Saw your cart come home loaded. Good week? | Your cook threw out a whole ham yesterday. A whole ham! | Your new windows catch the sun lovely. Catch me in the eye at dawn, mind.
remember pair: nb=envy 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

## A neighbour again (a day or two on)

rule n7_nb_again_ladder
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.mem.lent=ladder
priority 1
cooldown 2d
say The ladder. Still. | I've had to borrow a ladder from across the way to get my own ladder back. Not really. Nearly. | I'm not going to mention the ladder. I'm mentioning it.
remember pair: nb=borrow 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_again_pot
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.mem.lent=pot
priority 1
cooldown 2d
say The pot. Still at yours, is it? | I've been making stew in a bucket. Think on that. | I'm not going to mention the pot. I'm mentioning it.
remember pair: nb=borrow 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_again_saw
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.mem.lent=saw
priority 1
cooldown 2d
say Don't think I didn't see my saw on your woodpile. | The saw. You know the one. | My shelf's still on the floor, waiting for my saw.
remember pair: nb=borrow 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_again_noise
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.mem.nb=noise
priority 1
cooldown 2d
say Again last night! What are you building in there? | I've put a pillow on my side of the wall. Didn't help. | Same again last night. I counted the thumps. Forty.
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

rule n7_nb_again_ask
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.neighbours=yes pair.mem.nb=ask
priority 1
cooldown 2d
say Here's what I borrowed back, and a bit over for the trouble. | I've not forgotten what you lent me. Restday, I promise. | Thank you for the other day. Truly. It got us through.
remember pair: nb=repay 3d
remember pair: on=nb 1h
then other: town.neighbour

## The neighbour answers (self answers; pair.mem.nb says what about)

rule n7_na_plain
when concept=town.neighbour
say Ah. Right you are. | Is that so? | Well. There it is.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_noise
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=noise|walls
say Sorry. I'll see to it. | Ah. Sorry, #address#. It won't happen again. | Was it that loud? Gods. Sorry. | I'll put a rug down.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_noise_parent
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=noise|pups self.parent=yes self.age<=45
say Sorry. The little one had a dream and woke the house. | Teething. Gods help us all. Sorry. | They're pups, #address#. You were one.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_pups
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=pups
say I'll have a word with them. For all the good it'll do. | Sorry. They're wild this week. Something in the air. | Send them home with a flea in their ear. I'll back you.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_noise_short
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=noise|pups|walls self.temper=short
say It's my house. I'll bang about in it if I like. | You snore like a saw, so we're even. | Then move.
remember pair: na=rebuff 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_noise_merry
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=noise|walls self.humour=merry
say That was my dancing. I'll teach you, if you like. | I was practising for the festival. You'll thank me then. | Ha! Wait till you hear me on Restday.
remember pair: na=joke 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_noise_shy
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=noise|walls self.tone=shy
say Oh! Oh, gods. Sorry. I didn't know you could hear. | I'll put a rug down. Two rugs. | You heard that? All of it? Oh no.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_borrow
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=borrow
say Have I? Gods. I'll bring it round tonight. | Is that yours? I thought it was mine. | I was going to bring it back. I was just... still using it. | Tomorrow. First thing. Before the gulls.
remember pair: na=dodge 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_borrow_sly
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=borrow self.honesty=sly
say Are you sure you lent it to me? Lots of folk have one. | I thought that was a gift. | I'll swap you. You can have my old one. It's got character.
remember pair: na=dodge 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_ask_yes
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=ask
say Course. Wait there. | Take what you need. | Here. Don't fret over paying it back.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: na=give 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_ask_poor
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=ask self.wealth=poor|destitute
say I'd give it if I had it. We're scraping the pot ourselves. | I've a little. You can have half of it. | Ask me Restday. We're both #skint# till then.
remember pair: na=none 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_ask_cold
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=ask self.warmth=cold
say I'm not a shop. | Again? | You can have it. I'll be writing it down, mind.
remember pair: na=rebuff 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_ask_rich
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=ask self.wealth=rich
say Of course. I'll have it sent round. | Take what you need. Take more than you need. | My dear, think nothing of it.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: na=give 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_repay
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=repay
say There was no hurry. | Ah, you needn't have. Keep the extra. | That's what neighbours are for. | Any time. I mean it.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_repay_cold
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=repay self.warmth=cold
say Good. | About time. | I'd written it down, you know.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_fence
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=fence
say Halves, then. You buy the posts, I'll dig. | It was like that when I came. Ask the last lot. | I'll come and look at it Restday. Bring a mallet. | Aye, it's had its day, that fence.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_stair
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=stair
say Is it? I thought it was yours. | I'll see to it tonight. | Not mine. I'd know my own mess.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_fence_short
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=fence|stair|critter self.temper=short
say Not my doing. See to it yourself. | Always something with you. | I've better things to do.
remember pair: na=rebuff 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_garden
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=garden
say Ash and patience. And talking to them nicely. | It's all the rain. Nothing to do with me. | You'll have some when they're ready. There's always too many.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_garden_proud
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=garden self.job=farmer|herder|cook
say It's the soil. I bring it up from the river. I'll not say which bit. | Three generations of muck in that patch. | Secret. If I told you, you'd win the festival marrow.
remember pair: na=joke 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_harvest
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=harvest
say Eat all you like. There's too many for us. | Fair's fair. Bring me a few onions and we're square. | That tree's older than both houses. It goes where it likes.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_help
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=help
say You're a good neighbour. | Thank you. I mean it. | I'd do the same for you. I'll have to, now.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: na=thanks 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_help_proud
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=help|charity self.temper=short
say I can manage. | I'm not dead yet, thank you. | I'll do it myself, thank you. I'm not made of glass.
remember pair: na=proud 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_charity
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=charity
say You're kind. I'll not forget it. | I... thank you. I'll pay you back when I can. | Bless you. We'll eat tonight.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: na=thanks 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_charity_proud
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=charity self.warmth=cold|reserved self.wealth=poor|destitute
say I don't need charity. | We're managing. | Leave it on the step. I'll see.
remember pair: na=proud 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_charity_devout
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=charity self.piety=devout
say The Bright One sees what you do. So do I. | Bless you. Bless your house. | I'll light a candle for you on Restday.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: na=thanks 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_grief
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=grief
say Thank you. I can't... thank you. | The house is so quiet. Knock anyway, sometimes. | You're kind. You were always kind to them too.
remember pair: na=grief 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_critter
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=critter
say One of mine? I'll come and see. | It's not mine. I'd know. Probably. | I'll speak to it. It won't listen.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_cooking
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=cooking
say My granddam's recipe. I'll bring you a bowl. | Come round tomorrow and I'll make it again. | It's only onions and patience. And a bone. And a secret.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_trade
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=trade
say It's the work. I wash every night and it's still there. | Honest work, that smell. | I'll leave the boots out back. Sorry.
remember pair: na=sorry 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_away
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=away
say I'll watch it like it's mine. | Hens fed, door checked. Off you go. | I'll sit on your step with a rolling pin.
remember pair: na=promise 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_new
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=new
say Thank you. It's all boxes and confusion. | We'll be quiet. Mostly. | Kind of you. Where's the well, and is the baker honest?
regard other: familiarity +1
remember pair: na=thanks 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_late
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=late
say Long day. Long night. Same as ever. | Can't settle. Don't know why. | Nobody you'd know.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_late_short
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=late self.temper=short
say Mind your own. | What's it to you? | Do you sit at the window all night?
remember pair: na=rebuff 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_suspect
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=suspect
say Whatever you've heard, you heard wrong. | Who's been talking? | Say it to my face, then. Oh, you just did. Well.
regard self: affinity -1
remember pair: na=glare 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_suspect_nervy
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=suspect self.temper=nervy
say It wasn't me. Truly. I swear on my mother. | Please don't tell the Watch. I've done nothing. | I know what they say. It's not true. It's not.
remember pair: na=plead 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_snub
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=snub
say Right. I'll tell the pups to fly past. | We'll try to be poorer more quietly. | Course. Wouldn't want to frighten the guests.
remember pair: na=rebuff 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_envy
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=envy
say We work for it, same as you. | Mm. It's been a fair year. | Come round the back sometime. There's always something going spare.
remember pair: na=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_na_envy_cold
when concept=town.neighbour pair.mem.nb=envy self.warmth=cold
say That's our business. | I'd thank you not to watch my door. | Quite.
regard self: affinity -1
remember pair: na=rebuff 1h
then other: town.close
